.TH LIGHTSOUT 1 "2026-11-14" "lightsout" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
lightsout \- politely quit every open app with one command
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B lightsout
.RI [ options ] " " [ app " ...]"
.br
.B lightsout keep
.IR app " ..."
.br
.B lightsout unkeep
.IR app " ..."
.br
.B lightsout completion
.IR shell
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B lightsout
asks every open app to quit, the same way as choosing Quit or clicking an
app's close button, so apps with unsaved work can ask you to save first.
It never force quits: an app still open after the timeout is left running
and listed at the end, and
.B lightsout
exits with status 1.
.PP
It keeps open the app you run it from, which it detects from its parent
processes (and asks about when it can't tell), plus the apps named as
arguments or in the config file.
.PP
On macOS it quits the apps in the Dock and closes Finder windows. On Linux
(X11) it closes the windows of each app with
.BR wmctrl (1).
On Windows it closes the apps on the taskbar and File Explorer windows.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-dry\-run
Show which apps would be asked to quit, without quitting anything.
.TP
.BR \-y ", " \-\-yes
Don't ask which app you are running from. If it can't be detected,
.B lightsout
stops without quitting anything.
.TP
.BI \-\-timeout " seconds"
How long to wait for each app to quit, from 1 to 300 seconds. The default
is 10.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show usage and exit.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Show the version and exit.
.PP
Any other argument starting with
.B \-
is an error (exit status 2), so a mistyped option never quits anything.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BI keep " app ..."
Add apps to
.B ignoredApps
in the config file, so they are always kept open.
.TP
.BI unkeep " app ..."
Remove apps from
.BR ignoredApps .
.TP
.BI completion " shell"
Print a completion script for
.BR bash ", " zsh ", " fish " or " powershell .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/lightsout/config.yml
YAML with
.B ignoredApps
(a list of app names to always keep open) and
.B ignoredUpdates
(true to skip the update check).
.B keep
and
.B unkeep
rewrite this file, so comments in it are lost.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 when every app quit (or for a dry run), 1 when an app is still open or
apps couldn't be listed, 2 for invalid arguments.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B lightsout \-\-dry\-run
See what would be quit.
.TP
.B lightsout Slack \(dqGoogle Chrome\(dq
Quit everything except Slack and Google Chrome.
.TP
.B lightsout keep Spotify
Never quit Spotify.
.SH SEE ALSO
https://github.com/abhisheksinha1506/lightsout
